WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.410 --> 00:00:05.200
Marvel fans across the globe are celebrating
that Spider-Man won't be making an abrupt

00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:09.400
exit from the Marvel Cinematic Universe, and
Tom Holland is right there with them.

00:00:09.740 --> 00:00:14.440
The star of Spider-Man: Far From Home joined
much of Twitter in reacting with pure elation

00:00:14.440 --> 00:00:18.511
to the news that Sony Pictures and Disney,
the parent company of Marvel Studios, have

00:00:18.511 --> 00:00:23.160
reached an agreement to keep the wall-crawler
in the Marvel Cinematic Universe for one more

00:00:23.160 --> 00:00:26.560
Spider-Man solo movie and another Marvel Studios
production.

00:00:27.150 --> 00:00:31.260
Thousands of fans have endured more than a
month of heartbreak as Spidey's future in

00:00:31.260 --> 00:00:33.340
the MCU has languished in limbo.

00:00:33.640 --> 00:00:34.980
"Leave Spider-Man alone!

00:00:34.980 --> 00:00:37.320
You gonna pick on a guy tryin' to save a bunch
of kids?"

00:00:37.720 --> 00:00:42.500
In recent weeks, the outlook for ol' web-head's
potential return has been particularly grim.

00:00:43.040 --> 00:00:49.060
Sony Pictures chairman and CEO Tony Vinciquerra
publicly stated that, quote, "the door is

00:00:49.060 --> 00:00:53.050
closed" on re-upping the deal between the
two studios, and the recent news that Marvel

00:00:53.050 --> 00:00:58.289
Studios head honcho Kevin Feige would be hopping
across the hall to produce a Star Wars movie

00:00:58.289 --> 00:01:02.640
left many fans with the impression that he
only had time to do so because of the distinct

00:01:02.640 --> 00:01:04.800
absence of a third Spider-Man movie.

00:01:05.180 --> 00:01:07.960
This thankfully turned out not to be the case.

00:01:08.120 --> 00:01:10.200
Of course, Spidey fans are thrilled.

00:01:10.480 --> 00:01:15.470
In the immediate aftermath of the announcement
that Sony and Disney had agreed to play nice,

00:01:15.470 --> 00:01:20.580
Twitter absolutely exploded with an outpouring
of jubilation from fans and media outlets

00:01:20.580 --> 00:01:21.080
alike.

00:01:21.440 --> 00:01:22.640
"Okay, Spider-Man!

00:01:22.640 --> 00:01:23.760
Do a flip!"

00:01:24.540 --> 00:01:25.800
"Yeah!"

00:01:26.240 --> 00:01:27.380
"Not bad!"

00:01:27.720 --> 00:01:32.420
CinemaBlend posted a short clip of Peter Parker
disintegrating in the arms of Tony Stark near

00:01:32.420 --> 00:01:35.570
the end of Avengers: Infinity War, but in
reverse.

00:01:35.570 --> 00:01:36.260
The caption?

00:01:36.560 --> 00:01:38.520
"Mr. Stark, I feel good."

00:01:38.740 --> 00:01:41.240
Who knew young Peter was a James Brown fan?

00:01:41.760 --> 00:01:46.460
Another Twitter user posted fan art depicting
the famous scene from Spider-Man: Homecoming

00:01:46.470 --> 00:01:50.900
in which Spidey attempts to keep the Staten
Island Ferry from splitting in half using

00:01:50.900 --> 00:01:54.440
nothing but his webs, super-strength, and
sheer determination.

00:01:54.640 --> 00:01:58.300
In the rendering, the two halves of the ferry
are marked with banners featuring the respective

00:01:58.300 --> 00:02:01.780
logos of Sony and Disney, and the caption
reads,

00:02:02.120 --> 00:02:02.900
"Mr. Stark…

00:02:03.160 --> 00:02:04.300
I did it for you!!"

00:02:05.040 --> 00:02:08.860
Of course, the name and image of Parker's
late mentor was invoked early and often in

00:02:08.860 --> 00:02:10.040
all of the reactions.

00:02:10.280 --> 00:02:15.060
One that really got us was a still from Avengers:
Endgame in which a dozen different emotions

00:02:15.060 --> 00:02:20.260
are visible on Stark's face as he embraces
his young protege, who had just recently returned

00:02:20.260 --> 00:02:21.880
from being dusted for five years.

00:02:22.100 --> 00:02:22.680
The caption:

00:02:23.100 --> 00:02:24.260
"WE DID IT MR.

00:02:24.260 --> 00:02:24.780
STARK!

00:02:24.960 --> 00:02:25.960
WE DID IT SIR!"

00:02:26.360 --> 00:02:31.620
Another, similar still of mentor and mentee
embracing put the focus on Parker's face,

00:02:31.620 --> 00:02:32.460
along with the caption,

00:02:32.620 --> 00:02:33.960
"Welcome back, kid."

00:02:34.320 --> 00:02:38.000
Yes, this stuff kind of writes itself, but
that doesn't make it any less poignant.

00:02:38.640 --> 00:02:43.180
Some users took a slightly more subtle approach
to relaying their emotions, such as the one

00:02:43.180 --> 00:02:47.680
who posted a short clip of Thanos finally
relaxing after accomplishing his goal of wiping

00:02:47.680 --> 00:02:51.160
out half of all life in the universe at the
conclusion of Infinity War.

00:02:51.440 --> 00:02:52.500
Her caption read:

00:02:52.880 --> 00:02:57.180
"How I feel knowing that order is restored
and Spidey is back in the MCU."

00:02:57.720 --> 00:03:00.920
Others simply felt like partying, such as
the one who asked,

00:03:01.200 --> 00:03:03.220
"SPIDEY STANS, HOW ARE WE FEELING?"

00:03:03.420 --> 00:03:08.920
A series of four images followed: Thor: Ragnarok
director Taika Waititi raising a glass of

00:03:08.930 --> 00:03:13.970
wine, Holland looking like his mind has just
been blown, Hulk actor Mark Ruffalo swigging

00:03:13.970 --> 00:03:19.170
from what appears to be a gigantic bottle
of champagne, and Holland again looking completely

00:03:19.170 --> 00:03:22.540
blissed out in front of a background of dozens
of multicolored hearts.

00:03:22.930 --> 00:03:28.580
Meanwhile, Holland's Far From Home co-star
Zendaya chipped in with a low-res GIF of Spidey

00:03:28.580 --> 00:03:29.860
dancing his webs off.

00:03:30.420 --> 00:03:34.550
But as fans expected, the single greatest
reaction to the best news they've heard in

00:03:34.550 --> 00:03:36.460
a month came from Holland himself.

00:03:36.990 --> 00:03:41.520
The star posted a short clip from Martin Scorsese's
The Wolf of Wall Street featuring Leonardo

00:03:41.520 --> 00:03:46.490
DiCaprio as the notorious stockbroker Jordan
Belfort, to express his stance.

00:03:47.020 --> 00:03:47.680
"I'm not leavin'.

00:03:50.980 --> 00:03:51.480
I'm not leavin'.

00:03:54.100 --> 00:03:55.460
I'm not f---in' leavin!"

00:03:55.880 --> 00:03:57.660
And he even included fans' reaction:

00:04:02.600 --> 00:04:07.440
Holland's post was commented upon by a bevy
of celebrities, including Ruffalo, who wrote,

00:04:07.680 --> 00:04:08.620
"Back in a snap!

00:04:08.800 --> 00:04:10.580
Had a feeling we would see you again."

00:04:11.080 --> 00:04:16.580
Tony Revolori, who portrays Flash Thompson
in the Spidey solo films, commented, "Perfect!"

00:04:17.240 --> 00:04:22.109
But perhaps the best comment of all came from
none other than Dwayne "The Rock" Johnson,

00:04:22.109 --> 00:04:26.660
who summed up the feelings of every Spider-Man
fan on the planet today with only two words:

00:04:27.160 --> 00:04:27.660
"F---.

00:04:27.660 --> 00:04:28.160
Yes."

00:04:28.300 --> 00:04:30.200
We could not have said it better ourselves.

